# K18 COST GATES (docs/design/k18_memo_design.md §5 item 6; K18 fixed
# 2026-08-15). These blocks are here for their COMPILE TIME, not only for
# their spans — the correctness of the answers is guarded by the other three
# k18_*.rxt files, and what this one adds is that the two families whose cost
# the design lane had to bound cannot regress silently.
#
# They gate by riding the harness's own per-invocation pcrec budget
# (tests/lib/gen_timeout.sh `pcrec_timeout_secs`, 20 s plain / 60 s
# sanitizer), which is the mechanism D45 built and which K18's lane made
# axis-aware precisely so this would work. Exceeding it is a loud HARNESS
# FAILURE naming the case, never a hang.
#
# WHY THESE TWO FAMILIES, and neither is the obvious one:
#
# 1. THE FUZZ-FOUND CONSTANT-FACTOR WITNESS. The block below is the pattern
#    the repo's own differential fuzzer produced within 129 draws at seed 99,
#    and it is the one that caught a 7x constant-factor regression in the
#    design's first prototype: pcrec and the prototype did BYTE-IDENTICAL
#    work (332,476 closures, 15,743,238 states visited, maxdepth 1, 2
#    contexts) and the prototype still took 13.5 s against 0.62 s, all of it
#    one hash probe replacing one array access 15.7 million times. That is
#    what the empty-context fast path exists to prevent, and this pattern is
#    what would notice it going away. The `{8,8}` shrink beside it is the
#    same shape at a size that never nears the cap.
#
#    [SEL-1] (2026-08-28) WAS a `perr` block, is not any more. It has a live
#    capturing group, so `select_engine.c` already routes it to the VM for
#    the answer (`forces_captures`); what OVERFLOWED the DFA state cap
#    (>32,000 states) was the capture-erased forward+reverse pair auto builds
#    as the VM's PREFILTER (S6.1). Before [SEL-1] that overflow was a
#    refusal — every binary refused this pattern outright — which is exactly
#    the SPECIAL-CASE-SHAPED old contract [SEL-1] retired: under `auto` the
#    overflow is now a selection outcome (fall back to no prefilter), so the
#    pattern COMPILES, at RX_ENGINE "vm" / RX_VM_PREFILTER "none". The
#    COST-GATE claim this block exists for is UNCHANGED and, if anything,
#    sharper: the failed 32,000-state prefilter build still has to run to
#    completion before the fallback is even decided (compile.c's one-shot
#    retry, src/opt/select_engine.c's `forces_dfa_overflow`), so the same
#    ~0.68 s of real work is still paid on every compile of this pattern
#    (measured now: ~0.77 s total, the extra ~0.09 s being the cheap
#    no-prefilter VM build on the retry) — it is simply no longer thrown
#    away. Both `m`/`n` cases below are cheap on purpose (this block's job is
#    the COMPILE budget, not an exhaustive semantic sweep of the shape — the
#    `{8,8}` sibling and `tests/base/d27_*.rxt` already own that).
#
# 2. BOUNDED REPEAT x NULLABLE LOOP, swept in k. `A_REP` lowers `{0,k}` into
#    nested COPIES of the body, so the NFA grows with k (405 states at k=2,
#    1,485 at k=8) while the nesting a reader counts in the pattern does not
#    move at all. This family is why the honest cost variable is the number of
#    distinct open-loop CONTEXTS and not the loop-nesting depth a reader sees:
#    it runs at open depth 1 and was the family that made the design lane's
#    broken prototype 231x slower, invisible to any depth-based gate. On the
#    landed compiler it is LINEAR in k (measured 0.003 s at k=2, 0.009 s at
#    k=8).
#
# Every expectation generated from python3 `re` AND libpcre2 10.46, both
# oracles agreeing on every cell (D44's three-way rule).

# The fuzz-found witness: must compile inside the harness's pcrec budget
# (the DFA-cap-overflow build is real work, paid before the [SEL-1] fallback
# lands), and its two cases are oracle-verified rather than a bare `accept`
# — python3 `re` and libpcre2 10.46 agree on both (checked live this
# session: libpcre2 nomatch on "", match (0,1) on "a" — trivial cells by
# construction, since the alternative that answers them is the bare literal
# `a`, nowhere near any construct the two oracles are known to diverge on).
pattern (1{0,30}?[^]abc][^abc]){28,30}0+|a
n ""
m "a" 0 1

pattern (1{0,30}?[^]abc][^abc]){8,8}0+|a
n ""
m "a" 0 1
n "b"
n "c"
m "aa" 0 1
m "ab" 0 1
m "ac" 0 1
m "ba" 1 2
n "bb"
n "bc"
m "ca" 1 2
n "cb"
n "cc"
m "aab" 0 1
m "bab" 1 2
m "aba" 0 1

pattern ((?:(?:(?:[^a]{1,2}|[^a]??|.{0,2}?)+){0,2}(){2,3}){1,2}){2,3}
m "" 0 0
m "a" 0 0
m "aa" 0 0

pattern ((?:(?:(?:[^a]{1,2}|[^a]??|.{0,2}?)+){0,4}(){2,3}){1,2}){2,3}
m "" 0 0
m "a" 0 0
m "aa" 0 0

pattern ((?:(?:(?:[^a]{1,2}|[^a]??|.{0,2}?)+){0,6}(){2,3}){1,2}){2,3}
m "" 0 0
m "a" 0 0
m "aa" 0 0

pattern ((?:(?:(?:[^a]{1,2}|[^a]??|.{0,2}?)+){0,8}(){2,3}){1,2}){2,3}
m "" 0 0
m "a" 0 0
m "aa" 0 0
